course: dictionary
lesson: 4675
title: Hollow: empty, low, or not true
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Hollow has several meanings, and context tells you which one. «A lake is a body of water lying in a hollow of the land.» Water sits in the land, so a hollow here is a low dip in the ground, not an empty box.
explain: «Blakiston's fish owl needs old hollow trees by rivers to nest in.» A tree can be hollow, with an empty space inside it big enough for a nest. Ask: what word would fit here? Try "empty inside" in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Hollow can also describe something that is not sincere or not true. A hollow promise sounds nice but is not really meant. When a word has more than one meaning, swap each meaning into the sentence and keep the one that fits.
fact: Hollow means empty inside, with a space in it.
fact: A hollow is a hole in something, or a small low place in the ground.
fact: To hollow out something is to make a hole or space inside it, as people do with pumpkins at Halloween.
fact: «Hollow» can mean not sincere or not true, as in a hollow promise.
fact: Birds' bones are hollow, so they are light enough to fly, and a hollow tree trunk can be a home for owls and squirrels.
exercise: «A lake is a body of water lying in a hollow of the land.» What does hollow mean here? | A tall hill | A kind of fish | A wooden boat | *A low dip in the ground
exercise: «Blakiston's fish owl needs old hollow trees by rivers to nest in.» What does hollow mean? | Full of water | Made of stone | *Having an empty space inside | Very tall and thin
exercise: Dad says, «That promise was hollow.» What does hollow suggest? | Very heavy | *Not sincere or not true | Full of sweets | Loud and echoing
test: «Every corner of the world built its own instruments from what was at hand: gourds, termite-hollowed branches, bamboo, old oil drums.» What are termite-hollowed branches? | Branches that had fallen flat on the ground | *Branches with the inside eaten out, leaving a space | Branches painted gold | Branches cut into sticks for a fire
test: «A polar bear looks white, but each hair is see-through and hollow.» What does hollow tell us about each hair? | It is very thick and strong | It is made of metal | *It has an empty space inside | It is black all through
exam: Pupil says, «The hollow laugh fooled nobody.» What does hollow suggest? | *It sounded fake and not sincere | It echoed around the hall | It came from a hollow tree | It was loud and very happy
